      {
        "identifier": "https://www.isa-afp.org/entries/Ergodic_Theory.html",
        "note": "Sébastien Gouëzel, Ergodic Theory, Archive of Formal Proofs (Isabelle), 1 December 2015, with contributions from Manuel Eberl. Theory Recurrence proves kac_formula_nonergodic for conservative measure-preserving maps in a sigma-finite setting, with a natural-valued return time that is 0 off the recurrent subset; theory Ergodicity proves kac_formula in the ergodic case. It also proves the formula for induced functions, which is not done here. The step from one time to the next uses the same preimage identity as the proof here. The scopes differ: this statement drops conservativity and sigma-finiteness by letting the return time be infinite; the Isabelle entry covers induced functions.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/5feb6fc8c7f3c0842218f08f0d6b736e1c65ad40/CsdLean4/Mathlib/Dynamics/Kac.lean",
        "note": "My larger Lean project, where Kac's formula was added on 24 August 2026 (commit 1b15d3db): the ergodic probability case, as a series. This repository ports that file to Lean v4.35.0-rc3 and extends it with the general statement for any measure, the integral and average forms, and the first-hitting-set proof.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://prove2.me/theorems/d08379a7-654c-48e4-99e5-8d21df55e49e",
        "note": "MarkovMixing.kac_lemma by Shuze Chen on Prove2Me (22 August 2026): Kac's lemma for irreducible countable-state Markov chains with a stationary distribution, in Lean. A different setting. Its public page shows the statement, not the proof, so the proof was not checked here.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      }
